(d) whether any offence appears to have been committed and, if so, by whom;
(e) whether the accused has been arrested;
(f) whether he has been released on his bond and if so whether with or without sureties;
(g) whether he has been forwarded in custody under Section 170; and (h) whether the report of the medical examination of the woman has been attached where investigation relates to an offence under Sections 376, 376A, 376AB, 376B,
